3. ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS (ALWAYS)
====================================================================

Any use, copy, modification, or distribution of the Software, in
whole or in part, for Personal, Educational, or Commercial Use, must:

  (a) Include the following attribution in the README, documentation,
      footer, or another reasonably visible user-facing location:

        Based on Frakment by hanshapd
        https://github.com/hanshapd/frakment

  (b) Include this LICENSE file unmodified in all copies and
      derivative works.

  (c) Clearly mark any modified versions as modified, with a brief
      description of the changes (e.g., in a CHANGELOG or README).

====================================================================
4. COMMERCIAL USE REQUIREMENT
====================================================================

Before using the Software for any Commercial Use, you (or the legal
entity you represent) must have made one Qualifying Contribution as
defined in Section 1. This is the only path to Commercial Use.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
4.1  SCOPE OF SATISFACTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Once a Qualifying Contribution has been made, the requirement is
satisfied permanently for:

  - the individual who made the contribution, OR
  - the legal entity (company, organization, or team) on whose
    behalf the contribution was made,

for all future Commercial Use of the Software by that individual or
entity. No further contributions are required for future commercial
use by the same party.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
4.2  EVIDENCE ON REQUEST
--------------------------------------------------------------------

If hanshapd requests proof that the Commercial Use requirement has
been satisfied, you must provide, within 30 days, a link to the
merged pull request on GitHub.

Refusal or failure to provide evidence on request voids the
permission for Commercial Use until evidence is provided.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
4.3  NO REQUIREMENT FOR NON-COMMERCIAL USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Personal Use and Educational Use do NOT require a Qualifying
Contribution. Attribution (Section 3) is the only requirement for
those uses.

